    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (79.74) headlining the lineup as our most valuable asset. Facing a favorable matchup against Sugano (4.73 xERA), **Trea Turner**\u2019s elite speed and top-of-the-order placement provide the highest floor in our 5x5 format, where SB scarcity remains our primary focus. **Kyle Schwarber** (75.71) and **Yordan Alvarez** (68.59) also grade as elite starts; **Yordan Alvarez** manages to remain a high-tier play despite a lefty-on-lefty matchup, buoyed by his elite 0.428 xwOBA, while **Kyle Schwarber** benefits from similar favorable park conditions and a prime #2 slot. **Dillon Dingler** (60.99) and **Junior Caminero** (61.74) round out our strong starts, with **Dillon Dingler** notably seeing a significant 14-point boost from our dynamic platoon modeling against the projected start from Noah Cameron.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Chase Meidroth**, who flirted with the threshold but ultimately landed on the bench with a 35.64 score. Despite a decent base projection, his matchup against the formidable Logan Gilbert (3.09 xERA) pushed his efficiency well below our required 40.0 floor, effectively neutralizing his platoon advantage. Risks persist elsewhere, particularly for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (49.80), who draws the unenviable task of facing deGrom. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong**\u2019s profile is inflated by a dynamic platoon advantage and his essential speed profile, his score is severely hampered by deGrom\u2019s elite skill; he remains a marginal start strictly for his SB potential. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Carson Benge**; should these projections fluctuate upon official release, our efficiency scores will be recalibrated to ensure no player drops below our strict usage floor.",
